---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>CrackStreams Copyright Notice – DMCA Requests & Rights Information</title>
<meta name="description" content="Review CrackStreams guidance for copyright-related matters, including how rights owners can submit a DMCA request and provide relevant details about disputed material." />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>
<body>

  <header class="top-header">
    <a href="/" class="top-header-title">CrackStreams</a>
  </header>

<main class="page-container static-content-page">

  <div class="static-content-card">

    <h1 class="static-page-title">CrackStreams Copyright & DMCA Information</h1>

    <p class="static-page-subtitle">Revised: September 2026</p>

    <section class="static-section">

      <h2>1. Intellectual Property Matters</h2>

      <p>
        CrackStreams respects the intellectual property interests of copyright owners, creators, leagues, sporting bodies, broadcasters, publishers, and other rights holders. The website is presented as a sports information resource and is not designed to operate as a permanent storage facility for copyrighted audiovisual programming.
      </p>

      <p>
        CrackStreams does not independently create, upload, maintain, or archive live broadcasts or recorded video files on its own servers. References to external media, players, or other resources may involve independently managed third-party websites that operate separately from CrackStreams.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section class="static-section">

      <h2>2. Submitting a Copyright Concern</h2>

      <p>
        A copyright owner or an authorized representative may contact CrackStreams when they believe that a referenced item requires attention. To make a submission easier to evaluate, the request should provide clear and sufficiently detailed information about the material and the concern being raised.
      </p>

      <p>
        Copyright-related communications should, where applicable, include:
      </p>

      <ul class="static-list">

        <li>A clear description of the protected work involved.</li>

        <li>The webpage, reference, or location associated with the material in question.</li>

        <li>The sender's full name and dependable contact information.</li>

        <li>An explanation of why the material is believed to infringe applicable rights.</li>

        <li>Confirmation that the information provided is accurate to the best of the sender's knowledge.</li>

        <li>Information demonstrating ownership of the relevant rights or authorization to represent the rights owner.</li>

        <li>A valid written or electronic signature where appropriate.</li>

      </ul>

    </section>

    <section class="static-section">

      <h2>3. How to Reach CrackStreams</h2>

      <p>
        Copyright-related communications can be submitted through the <a href="/contact" class="inline-link">CrackStreams Contact Page</a> or sent directly to the contact address listed below:
      </p>

      <p class="contact-email-box">
        Email: <strong>crackstreams.contact@gmail.com</strong>
      </p>

      <p>
        Each communication may be considered based on the information supplied and the circumstances described by the sender. CrackStreams may review the available details before determining what response, if any, is appropriate.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section class="static-section">

      <h2>4. Third-Party Resources</h2>

      <p>
        Certain sports-related references, links, embedded tools, or external media resources may direct visitors to services operated by separate third parties. Those providers are responsible for the material distributed through their respective platforms and for addressing rights issues concerning content under their control. CrackStreams does not claim ownership of third-party broadcasts, recordings, trademarks, team marks, logos, or other protected works.
      </p>

    </section>

  </div>

</main>
</body>
</html>